description:
Duties Description The New York State Education Department’s (NYSED) Office of the Chief Financial Officer is seeking candidates for a Purchasing Agent position in the Contract Administration Unit. This Unit is responsible for the Department’s procurement, grant-making, and contracting processes. Duties of this position include, but are not limited to, the following:



* Review purchasing requisitions submitted by program offices. Determine the correct procurement method in accordance with State Finance Law, OGS guidelines, and NYSED internal procedures;
* Identify when centralized contracts, discretionary purchases, RFQs, sole source, or emergency procurements are appropriate;
* Develop detailed specifications, bid requirements, scopes of work, and complex RFQs;
* Conduct market research to identify qualified vendors, pricing, and product availability;
* Review vendor quotations and assist in evaluation processes. Respond to vendor inquiries related to solicitations, specifications, or procurement rules. Coordinate the preparation, issuance, and tracking of formal and informal solicitations;
* Recommend vendor selections in accordance with statutory and policy requirements;
* Prepare purchase orders and ensure all required documentation is complete for internal and external review;
* Maintain procurement records consistent with audit and retention requirements;
* Provide direction and daily oversight to the Assistant Purchasing Agent. Provide guidance and training to internal staff on purchasing processes;
* Review and approve RFQs, requisition analyses, and purchasing documents prepared by the Assistant Purchasing Agent;
* Assist the Senior Purchasing Agent with complex or time sensitive procurement initiatives;
* Ensure adherence to MWBE/SDVOB requirements, statutory thresholds, and internal controls;
* Stay current on changes in procurement laws, OGS guidance, and statewide purchasing policies; and
* Recommend improvements to NYSED purchasing procedures and workflows.

Minimum Qualifications NY HELPS

This title is part of the New York Hiring for Emergency Limited Placement Statewide Program (NY HELPS).


For the duration of the NY HELPS Program, this title may be filled via a non-competitive appointment, which means no examination is required but all candidates must meet the minimum qualifications of the title for which they apply. At a future date (within one year of permanent appointment), it is expected employees hired under NY HELPS will have their non-competitive employment status converted to competitive status, without having to compete in an examination. Employees will then be afforded with all of the same rights and privileges of competitive class employees of New York State. While serving permanently in a NY HELPS title, employees may take part in any promotion examination for which they are qualified.


NON-COMPETITIVE MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS:

To be considered for appointment through NY HELPS candidates must meet the open-competitive minimum qualifications for this position. The qualifications are:


* Six years of purchasing experience which includes being responsible for the purchase of a wide variety of supplies, materials, equipment, and services.

Substitution: An associate degree may substitute for two years of experience; a bachelor’s degree may substitute for four years of experience; a master’s degree may substitute for five years of experience; and a doctorate may substitute for six years of experience.


PROMOTION: Current NYSED employees must have one year of permanent competitive service as an Assistant Purchasing Agent or Office Assistant 3 (Calculations).


COMPETITIVE MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS:


Eligible List Appointment: Candidates must be reachable on the Civil Service eligible list for this title. If you are on the Civil Service eligible list for this title, you may receive a canvass letter. You must complete and return it as instructed on the letter.


55b/c Appointment: This position is eligible for 55b/c designation and candidates with 55b/c eligibility are encouraged to apply. Candidates must possess a current 55b/c eligibility letter and meet the minimum qualifications.


It is essential that candidates clearly and concisely indicate exactly how they meet the above minimum qualifications in their resume. Failure to show how you meet the minimum qualifications above may result in disqualification and removal from consideration.

Additional Comments CONDITIONS OF EMPLOYMENT: This will be a permanent, competitive or non-competitive appointment. Verification of experience and/or education will be required at the time of interview for all candidates. For 55b/c appointment, candidates must possess the minimum qualifications, a current 55b/c eligibility letter and are subject to verification of applicant eligibility. Promotions and transfers may change appointees’ negotiating unit. Candidates should be aware that changes in negotiating un

Duties Description The Office of Mental Health (OMH) is recruiting to fill a Assistant Purchasing Agent, Grade 14/Purchasing Agent Trainee, NS, positions within the Office of Financial Management, Bureau of Procurement Enterprise Services. The Bureau of Procurement Enterprise Services (BPES) provides contract management and procurement services to 24 facilities, OMH Central Office, OMH Cook Chill Production Center, and OMH Capital Operations.


The incumbent will be responsible for conducting, overseeing, and providing guidance on purchasing activities, operations, policies, and laws, rules and regulations for OMH Central Office and Psychiatric Centers. Specific duties may include, but are not limited to, the following:



* Assist in the development of bid documents and administering the solicitation and evaluation processes;



* Conduct Request for Proposals, Invitation for Bids, and Request for Quotes to obtain goods and services;



* Review/monitor and track assigned workload by using internal databases, project management tools, and SharePoint records as required;



* Perform a variety of functions related to contract management;



* Assist with special assignments and projects related;



* Purchase goods and services using appropriate procurement methodologies;



* Conduct analysis for establishing Minority and Women-owned Business Enterprise (MWBE) and Service-disabled Veteran Business Enterprise (SDVOB) goals for contract and purchases;



* Analyze data and prepare reports for internal and external stakeholders;



* Utilize the Statewide Financial System (SFS) for contract and purchase transactions;



* Other duties as assigned.

Minimum Qualifications Non-Competitive Minimum Qualifications Under the NY HELPS Program: This position includes an opportunity to serve in a traineeship, and applicants will be appointed to the appropriate level based on their education and/or experience.



* Purchasing Agent Trainee (starting salary $53,132): Four years of purchasing experience which includes being responsible for the purchase of a wide variety of supplies, materials, equipment, and services.
* Assistant Purchasing Agent (starting salary $56,183): Five years of purchasing experience which includes being responsible for the purchase of a wide variety of supplies, materials, equipment, and services.


An associate degree in a related field may substitute for two years of experience; A bachelor's degree in a related field may substitute for four years of specialized experience.  



Transfer Opportunity:

Candidates must have permanent status as an Assistant Purchasing Agent, Grade 14, and be eligible for lateral transfer; OR be eligible to transfer via Section 70.1 of the Civil Service Law to Assistant Purchasing Agent or Purchasing Agent Trainee.

Additional Comments The Bureau of Procurement Enterprise Services is conveniently located in independent offices on the grounds of the Capital District PC at 75 New Scotland Avenue, Albany, New York.


The starting salary for this position will vary based on the selected candidate’s education and/or experience. Candidates appointed at a trainee level will be required to successfully complete the traineeship to advance to the full performance level title and salary:


$53,132 (Purchasing Agent Trainee)

$56,183 (Assistant Purchasing Agent, full performance level)


For current New York State employees, the starting salary is based on the candidate’s salary at the time of hire.


Specific scheduled hours and telecommuting availability for this position will be discussed during the interview process. Please note, employees are required to apply and obtain approval through management to telecommute according to operational needs and Agency Telecommuting Program Guidelines.


The Mission of the New York State Office of Mental Health is to promote the mental health of all New Yorkers, with a focus on providing hope and supporting recovery for adults with serious mental illness and children with serious emotional disturbances. Applicants with lived mental health experience are encouraged to apply. OMH is deeply committed to supporting underserved individuals, organizations, and communities. To this end, OMH is focused on implementing activities and initiatives to reduce disparities in access, quality, and treatment outcomes for underserved populations. A critical component of these efforts is ensuring OMH is a diverse and inclusive workplace where all employees' unique attributes and skills are valued and utilized to support the mission of the Agency. OMH is an equal opportunity/affirmative action employer.  



This title is part of the New York Hiring for Emergency Limited Placement Statewide Program (NY HELPS). For the duration of NY HELPS, this title maybe filled via a non-competitive appointment, which means no examination is required but all candidates must meet the minimum qualification

**WHO WE ARE**

Biofire Technologies is on a mission to give gun owners better tools for reducing preventable gun injuries and deaths, especially among children. We believe our technology, combined with a best-in-class customer experience, will define the future of firearms safety for the next generation. Our mission-driven approach has earned support from the firearm community, the tech world, and the media.

Biofire employees encompass a diverse range of talents, including world-class engineers who have designed and tested firearms, medical devices, robots, cars, satellites, rockets, and supersonic jets; expert technicians from aerospace, defense tech, special forces, and gunsmithing; and elite operators from high-tech, advanced manufacturing, and regulated industries. Whether building the product or powering the company behind it, every Biofire team member is united by an obsession with safety, reliability, and operational excellence.

**OUR CULTURE**

Reducing accidental firearm injuries and deaths requires original thinking and authentic collaboration, so we’re deeply invested in building a team and culture that can achieve our mission together. Team members enjoy autonomy and flexibility from day one, so expect to be immediately tasked with solving challenging problems and building new systems that work. We’ll hold you accountable for executing audacious goals, giving and receiving honest feedback, and helping your teammates succeed. You’ll receive respect, kindness, and support from every direction while you figure out how to get it all done.

**ABOUT THE ROLE**

As a Senior Commodity Manager, Mechanical at Biofire, you will play a pivotal role in building the mechanical supply base that carries our product from low-rate initial production (LRIP) into full-rate production. You will own the mechanical commodity strategy across machining, injection molding, metal injection molding (MIM), and metals fabrication — qualifying suppliers, driving cost out of the bill of materials, de-risking single-source exposure, and formalizing the commercial agreements that will carry Biofire through its next phase of growth. We are looking for someone who pairs strong mechanical manufacturing process knowledge with pragmatic system-building instincts and the ability to influence engineering, quality, and production partners without direct authority, to help our supply chain team scale procurement infrastructure from scratch.

To succeed you will need to be able to stand up a supplier qualification framework, a dual-sourcing roadmap, and formal commercial agreements within your first six months, all while keeping current production supply uninterrupted. You will need to be a pragmatic, hands-on system builder who is eager to take a nascent, LRIP-stage mechanical supply base and turn it into a qualified, cost-optimized, and resilient supply chain capable of supporting Biofire’s production ramp. If you’re excited about helping to solve mission-critical challenges, we encourage you to apply.

**KEY RESPONSIBILITIES**

Day-to-day responsibilities of the role will include:

* Design and implement a supplier qualification framework (PPAP, first-article inspection, capacity audits) calibrated by commodity type, and drive Biofire’s mechanical supplier base through qualification for full-rate production;
* Drive a significant reduction in mechanical BOM cost through DFX-driven process conversions (e.g., machined-to-molded), volume-based renegotiation, competitive bidding, and improved commercial terms, tracked in a supplier-confirmed savings tracker;
* Evaluate the full mechanical parts portfolio to identify single-source risk, build a prioritized dual-sourcing roadmap, and drive qualification of second sources based on risk, business impact, and total cost of ownership;
* Negotiate and formalize MSAs and/or stocking agreements with mechanical suppliers covering pricing, payment terms, lead-time commitments, and quality expectations, delivering term sheets ready for leadership and legal approval;
* Own supply continuity through the production ramp — proactively monitor supplier capacity, translate production schedules into supplier demand signals, and prevent line-down events due to preventable mechanical supply gaps;
* Participate actively in DFX design reviews alongside mechanical engineering, applying process knowledge across MIM, injection molding, machining, and metals fabrication to flag manufacturability, cost, and quality risks before parts are released for sourcing;
* Build and maintain a mechanical supply chain roadmap aligned to Biofire’s product roadmap and production ramp plan, anticipating supplier capacity constraints and category-specific market dynamics;
* Coach and develop buyers on supplier capability assessment, holistic quote evaluation, and scorecard input, building capability across the broader procurement team.

**QUALIFICATIONS**

